@2reb_fl 
Every DeFi risk question boils down to one: will this protocol be able to pay what it owes? That's solvency, and Risk Pricing is where the market puts a number on it.

It's a word people already trust from insurance and credit ratings, and it says what the tool does in one go, just like Deep and Futarchy. solvency.seer.pm.

@italeeex

Margin is the cushion between a price and the loss it can absorb: the room a trader keeps before a position turns into damage. A market-implied risk price is exactly that number, it measures how much room each DeFi asset has before its risk reaches you. The word is the one people already use, so it needs no lesson.

