@italeeex

Basis is the gap the market prices between two things that are not the same, and risk pricing is that gap made visible: how far the market's estimate for an asset sits from what its holders treat as normal. Traders already read basis as the number that says which way a market leans, so the name arrives with its meaning attached.

Илья, веб-разработчик

@italeeex

A Plimsoll mark is the line painted on a hull that shows the most it may safely carry, and crossing it is how a ship becomes overloaded. A risk price does the same job for a DeFi asset: it marks the level the market is willing to underwrite before the position turns into a loss. It is a threshold rather than a forecast, which is what a tool comparing market estimates of risk should be.

Илья, веб-разработчик

@italeeex

Ballast is the weight a vessel carries low in the hull so it stays steady in bad water. A risk price reads the same way: it shows the downside a position absorbs before it starts to tip, for each DeFi asset the market is pricing. The name says the tool is about staying level rather than predicting the weather.

Илья, веб-разработчик

@italeeex

A keel is the line running under a hull that everything else is balanced against, and it keeps a vessel upright in a seaway. Risk pricing is that reference line for DeFi assets: one level to measure every estimate against, so two markets can be compared honestly. The word says the product provides the baseline rather than another opinion.

Илья, веб-разработчик

@italeeex

A haircut is the discount the market applies to an asset because of the risk it carries; traders already use the word for exactly this. Naming the interface after the number it shows makes it self-explaining: you are looking at everyone's haircut, side by side. Finance-native and impossible to confuse with Deep.

Илья, веб-разработчик

@italeeex

A bench is where things are put side by side to be compared, and a benchmark is the number the rest is judged against. Risk Pricing is that flat surface: every DeFi asset's market-implied risk on one line. Short, unpretentious, and the product's job is obvious from the word.

Илья, веб-разработчик

@italeeex

A ship's waterline turns a hull full of assumptions into one visible fact: how much it is carrying. This interface draws that line under every protocol and lets you see whose sits higher. Plain word, physical image, and it pairs with Deep (depth) without saying the same thing.

Илья, веб-разработчик

@italeeex

A weather vane does not forecast the weather, it shows which way it is turning, at a glance, before you commit to anything. Risk Pricing does that for DeFi: direction and relative pressure on every asset, visible side by side. One syllable, one image, no jargon.

