@italeeex

A sextant fixes your position by comparing bearings to several known points instead of trusting one reading. That is what this interface does with risk: it prices each protocol against the others, so a single yes-or-no number stops being the whole story. Short, instrument-grade, and it sits beside Deep and Futarchy without repeating them.

